⏺ Plan: scripts/debug_rebounds_player.py                                                                                                    
                                         
  ---                                                                                                                                       
  Process
                                                                                                                                            
  Goal: Given a player name + season, show every artifact they touch in the rebounds pipeline so you can trace why any feature is NA or
  wrong.                                                                                                                                    
  
  Three sections of output, in pipeline order:                                                                                              
                                                            
  Section 1 — Raw game logs                                                                                                                 
  Pull from s3://nba-api-mt/player_game_logs/{season}/*.csv via DuckDB glob. For each game that season: DATE, MIN, REB, FGA, FG3A, TEAM,
  GAME_ID. This tells you whether source data is missing entirely (player not in logs) or FG3A is zero/null across all games (explains      
  roll_fg3a_mean_20 = NA).                                  
                                                                                                                                            
  Section 2 — Input universe                                                                                                                
  Pull from s3://nba-betting-mt/rebounds/input/rebounds_input_universe.parquet. Filter to player + season. Show: date, game_id, REB,
  spread_signed, team_normalized, home_team_norm, away_team_norm, plus the raw audit columns (input_spread_by_side, input_fg3a_tail_20).    
  This tells you whether the spread join failed, and whether FG3A is actually being read.
                                                                                                                                            
  Section 3 — Feature universe                              
  Pull from s3://nba-betting-mt/rebounds/features/rebounds_feature_universe.parquet. Filter to player + season. Show: date, game_id, all 6
  B_MIN_MAX_FEATS + all 5 B_MIN_MAX_AUDIT_LIST_COLS. Flag each NaN explicitly. This is what the model sees.                                 
  
  At the end, print a NA summary: for each feature column, count how many of that player's rows are null and why (cross-referenced against  
  sections 1 and 2).                                        
                                                                                                                                            
  ---                                                       
  Coding plan
             
  File: scripts/debug_rebounds_player.py
                                                                                                                                            
  Args:
  - --player "Jamal Cain" — raw name, normalized internally                                                                                 
  - --season 2025-26                                                                                                                        
  - --as-of-date YYYY-MM-DD (optional) — if passed, filter feature/input universe to a single game date
                                                                                                                                            
  Dependencies:                                                                                                                             
  - src/io_utils.py → read_parquet_any for input + feature universe
  - src/nba_rebounds_modeling/duckdb_s3_creds.py → connect_duckdb_s3 for game log glob                                                      
  - src/player_team_history/name_normalization.py → normalize_from_odds_api for name matching
  - src/nba_rebounds_modeling/rebounds_feature_spec.py → B_MIN_MAX_FEATS, B_MIN_MAX_AUDIT_LIST_COLS, GROUP_KEYS                             
                                                                                                                                            
  Structure:                                                                                                                                
                                                                                                                                            
  parse_args()                                                                                                                              
  normalize_player_name(raw) → player_normalized            
                                                                                                                                            
