    → filter player + season (+ date if passed)                                                                                             
    → print table: date | game_id | REB | spread_signed | team_normalized | input_spread_by_side | input_fg3a_tail_20                       
    → flag rows where spread_signed is null                                                                                                 
                                                                                                                                            
  section_3_feature_universe(player_normalized, season, as_of_date=None)
    → read_parquet_any(s3://nba-betting-mt/rebounds/features/rebounds_feature_universe.parquet)                                             
    → filter player + season (+ date if passed)                                                                                             
    → print table: date | game_id | [B_MIN_MAX_FEATS] | [B_MIN_MAX_AUDIT_LIST_COLS]
    → for each column: flag NaN count                                                                                                       
                                                                                                                                            
  print_na_summary(logs_df, input_df, feat_df)
    → for each NA in feature universe: cross-ref to input universe and logs to explain root cause                                           
                                                                                                                                            
  Name matching: normalize --player with normalize_from_odds_api, then filter both parquets on player_normalized == normalized_name. For the
   DuckDB game log query, do a LOWER(PLAYER_NAME) LIKE '%cain%'-style match since game log names are raw NBA API strings, then verify       
